WEBVTT

00:00:11.386 --> 00:00:15.849
Wh-What's with the serious faces, you two?

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:19.394
I've got a bad feeling about this.

00:00:19.394 --> 00:00:22.022
But go ahead. Tell me what you want.

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:24.942
Kozakura, we need your help!

00:00:24.942 --> 00:00:29.154
Y-You guys can go to the Otherside
all you want. Just leave me out--

00:00:29.154 --> 00:00:30.864
Yeah.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.533
We know.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:40.165
We're here to launch a rescue operation
for the U.S. forces at Kisaragi Station.

00:00:40.165 --> 00:00:43.544
A rescue operation?

00:00:58.141 --> 00:01:02.479
<i>School never taught me what friends are</i>

00:01:02.479 --> 00:01:07.860
<i>People are such difficult creatures</i>

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:12.281
<i>This world where you never</i>
<i>know what's said behind your back</i>

00:01:12.281 --> 00:01:17.828
<i>Looks a little ugly to me</i>

00:01:17.828 --> 00:01:22.708
<i>Compassion and ego sway on the scales</i>

00:01:22.708 --> 00:01:27.254
<i>They've swayed ever since I met you</i>

00:01:27.254 --> 00:01:30.174
<i>Your trespassing did a number on me</i>

00:01:30.174 --> 00:01:34.469
<i>It's not like anyone would do</i>

00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:34.553
<i>Is your empathy and complicity just an act?</i>

00:01:34.553 --> 00:01:35.721
"Kisaragi"
"Katasu - Yami"
<i>Is your empathy and complicity just an act?</i>

00:01:35.721 --> 00:01:39.975
<i>Is your empathy and complicity just an act?</i>

00:01:39.975 --> 00:01:44.313
<i>Like a fish out of water</i>

00:01:44.313 --> 00:01:46.607
<i>Delicacy and literacy</i>

00:01:46.607 --> 00:01:49.193
<i>Might not be necessary</i>

00:01:49.193 --> 00:01:52.362
<i>I just want to be wanted</i>

00:01:52.362 --> 00:01:54.781
<i>Selfish little me</i>

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:58.952
<i>The scales have tipped</i>

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.205
<i>As friends</i>

00:02:01.205 --> 00:02:07.211
<i>Let's meet in a secret place</i>

00:02:14.843 --> 00:02:16.970
Our map of the Otherside

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.933
is actually useful now, thanks to you, Kozakura.

00:02:20.933 --> 00:02:22.809
So you're serious about this?

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:26.396
We are. And I don't want to go at night again.

00:02:26.396 --> 00:02:29.650
If we're gonna try,
lunchtime is our only chance.

00:02:30.901 --> 00:02:33.362
You're dealing with foreign soldiers.

00:02:33.362 --> 00:02:38.075
Even if you rescue them, you may end up
in more trouble than you bargained for.

00:02:38.075 --> 00:02:40.744
We can't just abandon them.

00:02:40.744 --> 00:02:42.913
I can't get them out of my mind.

00:02:42.913 --> 00:02:45.541
Yeah, I get it, but how?

00:02:45.541 --> 00:02:49.419
There's no guarantee you'll reach their camp.

00:02:49.419 --> 00:02:54.091
We ended up on the
Otherside after visiting this café.

00:02:54.091 --> 00:02:56.051
Maybe we can get there from here.

00:02:56.051 --> 00:03:00.138
So you only went to
the Otherside once from here?

00:03:00.138 --> 00:03:02.724
That's right. And here's why.

00:03:05.352 --> 00:03:07.563
It was this hat.

00:03:07.563 --> 00:03:11.441
You can't know that for sure.

00:03:11.441 --> 00:03:15.946
The issue might be with the entrance
or exit, or even this place itself.

00:03:15.946 --> 00:03:19.324
If that were true, wouldn't
all the customers disappear?

00:03:19.324 --> 00:03:23.620
Hmph. Maybe it's you guys.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:27.958
You've been to Otherside so many times,
maybe entrances readily gravitate to you.

00:03:27.958 --> 00:03:32.754
You'll have to leave us here
if we want to find out.

00:03:32.754 --> 00:03:36.884
Once you're gone, we'll put
on the hat and step outside.

00:03:36.884 --> 00:03:40.596
If you remain in this world,

00:03:40.596 --> 00:03:43.682
and Toriko and I end up on the Otherside,

00:03:43.682 --> 00:03:45.851
then I believe it's the hat.

00:03:45.851 --> 00:03:48.228
Is that why you brought me here?

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:53.775
N-No! You were the one
who said you wanted to join us.

00:03:56.445 --> 00:03:59.865
Whatever. If you can get
to the Otherside that way,

00:03:59.865 --> 00:04:03.577
I'll pay whatever you want for that hat...

00:04:04.703 --> 00:04:08.457
...assuming you make it back alive.

00:04:08.457 --> 00:04:11.293
I'll stop by Junkudo on the way home.

00:04:11.293 --> 00:04:14.296
Call me if it doesn't work.

00:04:14.296 --> 00:04:17.257
Do you think she wanted to head back with us?

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:18.133
--She's afraid of going back alone?

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:19.676
--Thank you!
--She's afraid of going back alone?

00:04:19.676 --> 00:04:22.804
I'd understand if it was dark,
but it's 1:00 in the afternoon.

00:04:22.804 --> 00:04:27.226
Maybe she's not afraid,
just a little uneasy all alone.

00:04:30.687 --> 00:04:33.899
Well, shall we? You ready?

00:04:33.899 --> 00:04:36.151
Ready.

00:04:38.946 --> 00:04:41.615
What are you doing?

00:04:41.615 --> 00:04:44.785
I'm not used to seeing you like that.

00:04:47.412 --> 00:04:52.417
It was cute in its own way,
not unlike a safari guide.

00:04:52.417 --> 00:04:54.795
Just stop, already.

00:04:54.795 --> 00:04:59.633
If we were trying to do it the same way
as last time, shouldn't I have put it on?

00:04:59.633 --> 00:05:03.762
Who knows whether the one who
puts the hat on might come to harm?

00:05:03.762 --> 00:05:09.434
You wore it once. Now it's my turn.
After that, we won't ever use it again.

00:05:16.859 --> 00:05:21.196
Last time, how long did it take
before we noticed a change?

00:05:21.196 --> 00:05:24.908
I put the hat on soon after we got to the café.

00:05:24.908 --> 00:05:27.786
Then we drank for three hours or so.

00:05:28.954 --> 00:05:30.914
Still no change.

00:05:30.914 --> 00:05:33.166
Yeah.

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:37.546
Maybe it didn't work this time. Sorry.

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:42.176
No.

00:05:42.176 --> 00:05:44.428
It looks like it did.

00:05:44.428 --> 00:05:46.221
Huh?

00:06:16.084 --> 00:06:20.172
Maybe we really should have brought the AP-1.

00:06:20.172 --> 00:06:23.425
That thing would've been useless in a battle.

00:06:23.425 --> 00:06:24.968
How about with a mechanical arm?

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:26.887
That wouldn't help.

00:06:26.887 --> 00:06:28.805
I was thinking.

00:06:28.805 --> 00:06:33.352
Will they even see this white flag?
Wouldn't yellow or orange be better?

00:06:33.352 --> 00:06:36.438
A yellow flag doesn't have the same meaning.

00:06:36.438 --> 00:06:39.775
I don't think the color really matters.

00:06:39.775 --> 00:06:44.821
I doubt they'll suddenly
start shooting, but just in case.

00:07:05.217 --> 00:07:06.802
They suddenly started shooting.

00:07:06.802 --> 00:07:09.930
Jeez! We almost got killed!

00:07:16.979 --> 00:07:20.566
How rude! We're here to rescue them!

00:07:20.566 --> 00:07:26.864
They're probably wondering
whether we're even human.

00:07:41.003 --> 00:07:42.504
SOS?

00:07:42.504 --> 00:07:49.052
It's the only Morse code I know.
I wish Mom had taught me more.

00:08:33.222 --> 00:08:35.307
You two again?

00:08:35.307 --> 00:08:36.600
Nice to see you.

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:39.811
Sorry it took so long,
but we're here to rescue you.

00:08:39.811 --> 00:08:44.942
You're still alive?
Where were you the past few days?

00:08:44.942 --> 00:08:46.360
A few days?

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:50.781
Maybe time doesn't go by
at the same rate between worlds.

00:08:52.199 --> 00:08:53.325
Listen.

00:08:53.325 --> 00:08:59.414
I want you to know that
despite my eye, I'm not a monster.

00:08:59.414 --> 00:09:01.625
Same with Toriko.

00:09:01.625 --> 00:09:03.919
I know.

00:09:03.919 --> 00:09:09.258
Our comrades who went insane
became extremely violent.

00:09:09.258 --> 00:09:12.219
So what was that about rescuing us?

00:09:15.055 --> 00:09:16.849
Over there!

00:09:24.731 --> 00:09:28.318
My right eye can spot glitches.

00:09:28.318 --> 00:09:32.573
I believe you call them bear traps.

00:09:37.452 --> 00:09:39.872
Um, where's Greg?

00:09:39.872 --> 00:09:44.626
He's... dead.

00:09:44.626 --> 00:09:48.172
He thought you'd been run over
and killed by the Meat Train,

00:09:48.172 --> 00:09:53.135
so he blew up part of the track,
taking out one of the train cars.

00:09:53.135 --> 00:09:57.806
But in the ensuing battle with
the apes that came rushing out...

00:09:59.057 --> 00:10:01.852
Don't let it weigh on you.

00:10:01.852 --> 00:10:06.857
He was already at the point
where he couldn't take anymore.

00:10:06.857 --> 00:10:12.154
How was he able to destroy an Otherside entity?

00:10:12.154 --> 00:10:17.367
You know, like how gunshots won't hit home
unless I'm watching with my right eye?

00:10:17.367 --> 00:10:23.248
Does going insane bring people
closer to the entities of this world?

00:10:25.167 --> 00:10:28.795
So then no more trains will be arriving.

00:10:28.795 --> 00:10:31.715
No, they're still coming.

00:10:44.394 --> 00:10:46.480
Major!

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:48.148
What are you two...?!

00:10:48.148 --> 00:10:52.027
The girls are back to rescue us.

00:10:52.027 --> 00:10:53.779
Huh?

00:10:54.863 --> 00:10:57.908
The girls?

00:11:17.511 --> 00:11:19.555
We can have all this?

00:11:19.555 --> 00:11:23.433
Yeah. We can't take most of it with us anyway.

00:11:23.433 --> 00:11:27.646
I see. So next time, we can come here and...

00:11:32.359 --> 00:11:33.527
What's that?

00:11:33.527 --> 00:11:35.320
Whoa.

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:37.239
Oh, these?

00:11:37.239 --> 00:11:41.451
The one with the big arm
on the front is the Gorgon.

00:11:41.451 --> 00:11:45.414
It's based on the Buffalo
mine-protected clearance vehicle.

00:11:45.414 --> 00:11:48.792
The armored bus behind it is the Owlbear.

00:11:48.792 --> 00:11:53.172
It's based on the RG-33L mine-resistant vehicle.

00:11:53.172 --> 00:11:57.217
They both have a doghouse
based on a modified OGPK,

00:11:57.217 --> 00:12:01.221
enabling attacks in all directions.

00:12:01.221 --> 00:12:04.308
We know it's all over
if we roll over a bear trap,

00:12:04.308 --> 00:12:07.644
but we made these as our one and final hope.

00:12:07.644 --> 00:12:10.689
They should prove useful with your help.

00:12:10.689 --> 00:12:14.151
I'm really glad you're here.

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:18.655
Th-They're amazing.

00:12:18.655 --> 00:12:20.199
Yeah, totally.

00:12:20.199 --> 00:12:23.035
Please wait right here.

00:12:23.035 --> 00:12:25.787
You think we should've acted more impressed?

00:12:25.787 --> 00:12:28.582
He looked satisfied enough.

00:12:28.582 --> 00:12:31.001
Lemme see your rifle.

00:12:33.128 --> 00:12:34.963
You're so good with your hands.

00:12:34.963 --> 00:12:37.466
It's easier than you think.

00:12:37.466 --> 00:12:41.220
Did your parents teach you
that, too? They're Canadian?

00:12:41.220 --> 00:12:43.847
Did I ever mention that?

00:12:43.847 --> 00:12:46.058
Oh, sorry. Kozakura told me.

00:12:46.058 --> 00:12:51.146
Oh, well, Mom taught me.
She was in the Canadian Armed Forces.

00:12:51.146 --> 00:12:52.731
All done.

00:12:53.774 --> 00:12:56.735
It's definitely lighter now.

00:12:56.735 --> 00:12:58.362
Right?

00:13:02.699 --> 00:13:04.868
Yeah, looking good!

00:13:04.868 --> 00:13:06.370
Is that a compliment?

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:08.539
Yeah, so just take it.

00:13:08.539 --> 00:13:11.375
If you say so.

00:13:11.375 --> 00:13:15.170
Now, let's go over how to hold it again.

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:18.423
Basically, you hold the
stock against your shoulder

00:13:18.423 --> 00:13:20.342
and aim with the scope.

00:13:20.342 --> 00:13:23.220
You can hold the handguard with your left hand,

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:25.597
or you can hold the foregrip.

00:13:25.597 --> 00:13:28.600
Some even hold it in front
of the magazine catch.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:30.894
Like this? Is this right?

00:13:30.894 --> 00:13:35.315
Don't stick your elbows out.
Maintain a more compact form.

00:13:35.315 --> 00:13:37.776
Hold your rifle like you're hiding behind it.

00:13:37.776 --> 00:13:40.904
Then act as if it's an extension of your arms,

00:13:40.904 --> 00:13:44.366
so your body and rifle move quickly in unison.

00:13:44.366 --> 00:13:49.246
It's longer than a handgun,
so keep an eye on where it's pointed.

00:13:49.246 --> 00:13:51.915
Good. Much better.

00:13:51.915 --> 00:13:53.917
And don't forget--

00:13:53.917 --> 00:13:58.005
Never put your finger on the
trigger unless you're gonna fire.

00:13:58.005 --> 00:14:00.841
Okay, good!

00:14:00.841 --> 00:14:04.803
Marines! Commence Operation Return Home!

00:14:04.803 --> 00:14:07.639
The girls will lead the way!

00:14:09.683 --> 00:14:12.978
Okay, marines, get ready to move out!

00:14:12.978 --> 00:14:14.980
Hoorah!

00:15:15.624 --> 00:15:16.708
Stop!

00:15:16.708 --> 00:15:18.836
Evade right!

00:15:22.005 --> 00:15:24.758
No! Stop!

00:15:24.758 --> 00:15:28.971
Cut the wheel much sharper right!

00:15:34.768 --> 00:15:37.938
We haven't even gone a hundred meters.

00:15:48.448 --> 00:15:50.742
Stop!

00:15:50.742 --> 00:15:53.495
Go right... 30 degrees.

00:15:53.495 --> 00:15:54.955
Roger.

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:01.670
Sorawo, are you okay?

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:05.132
Yeah, but at this rate...

00:16:05.132 --> 00:16:05.716
--That's it!

00:16:05.716 --> 00:16:06.258
--Huh?
--That's it!

00:16:06.258 --> 00:16:06.842
--Huh?
--Do you have a long object that could
extend beyond the driver-side windshield?

00:16:06.842 --> 00:16:10.929
--Do you have a long object that could
extend beyond the driver-side windshield?

00:16:12.055 --> 00:16:14.308
I'll take a look.

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:37.122
The camp!

00:16:38.957 --> 00:16:43.045
We blew it up to leave as few
traces of our presence as possible.

00:16:43.045 --> 00:16:45.422
What a waste.

00:16:53.597 --> 00:16:58.268
Are you sure you guys came from that forest?

00:16:58.268 --> 00:17:03.023
Most likely, based on the distance
and bearing from the camp.

00:17:03.023 --> 00:17:05.567
Then we're almost there.

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:18.539
Hey, look! Someone's coming!

00:17:18.539 --> 00:17:20.332
Who is it? Is it one of us?

00:17:20.332 --> 00:17:21.500
What is it?

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:23.669
They said someone's coming.

00:17:23.669 --> 00:17:25.546
Someone?

00:17:50.904 --> 00:17:52.364
They're not human! It's the enemy!

00:17:52.364 --> 00:17:54.950
Contact! Open fire!

00:18:09.673 --> 00:18:12.384
Get inside, quick! It's dangerous out here!

00:18:12.384 --> 00:18:14.511
No can do. I have to watch the enemy!

00:18:14.511 --> 00:18:17.472
Don't worry. We'll be fine!

00:18:17.472 --> 00:18:18.765
I'm right here.

00:18:18.765 --> 00:18:20.601
Thanks.

00:18:25.439 --> 00:18:27.065
This is a lousy position.

00:18:27.065 --> 00:18:29.776
Yeah, we gotta move.

00:18:38.869 --> 00:18:40.078
It's glitch-free!

00:18:40.078 --> 00:18:41.830
Bust through!

00:18:52.132 --> 00:18:54.092
Look out!

00:18:54.092 --> 00:18:55.469
Ouch!

00:18:55.469 --> 00:18:57.221
You okay, Sorawo?

00:18:57.221 --> 00:18:58.889
I think so.

00:19:00.015 --> 00:19:01.308
I don't understand.

00:19:01.308 --> 00:19:04.937
We're scoring direct hits
but dealing zero damage.

00:19:04.937 --> 00:19:07.731
We hit 'em hard before, so why not now?

00:19:10.609 --> 00:19:12.027
Got one!

00:19:13.237 --> 00:19:14.821
Over there!

00:19:14.821 --> 00:19:17.032
Got it!

00:19:17.032 --> 00:19:17.616
--Direct hit!

00:19:17.616 --> 00:19:18.992
--Yes!
--Direct hit!

00:19:18.992 --> 00:19:19.952
It's not over yet.

00:19:19.952 --> 00:19:21.078
Huh?

00:20:00.033 --> 00:20:01.577
Stop!

00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:24.183
It's a glitch or maybe a gate.

00:20:24.183 --> 00:20:26.935
Was this your entry point?

00:20:28.353 --> 00:20:32.441
Y-Yeah, I think it might have been.

00:20:32.441 --> 00:20:36.361
It does look familiar.

00:20:36.361 --> 00:20:39.823
This place has a distinctive look.
You think you'd remember it.

00:20:39.823 --> 00:20:45.037
Yeah, you'd think, but my memory
is all fuzzy for some reason.

00:20:49.249 --> 00:20:53.045
Wait, it's coming back now.

00:20:53.045 --> 00:20:57.049
Yes, we were definitely here.

00:20:57.049 --> 00:21:02.137
It was just a training mission,
but before we knew it, we ended up here.

00:21:02.137 --> 00:21:04.556
And then...

00:21:04.556 --> 00:21:07.059
I saw something.

00:21:07.059 --> 00:21:09.895
It was a nightmare.

00:21:11.230 --> 00:21:12.981
Wait here!

00:21:12.981 --> 00:21:15.025
We'll take a look.

00:21:20.197 --> 00:21:21.782
He's terrified.

00:21:21.782 --> 00:21:24.368
He said it was a nightmare.

00:21:24.368 --> 00:21:26.578
What happened here?

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:36.797
Could this be...?

00:21:36.797 --> 00:21:38.882
Sorawo?

00:21:55.691 --> 00:21:57.943
Kakandara.

00:21:58.026 --> 00:22:01.989
"Operation Rescue U.S. Forces"

00:22:11.623 --> 00:22:15.878
<i>My hair was tossed by the cold wind</i>

00:22:15.878 --> 00:22:20.007
<i>Did you notice me shut the window?</i>

00:22:20.007 --> 00:22:24.303
<i>I lose my nerve when we get so close</i>

00:22:24.303 --> 00:22:28.182
<i>I don't need something that won't last</i>

00:22:28.182 --> 00:22:30.309
<i>Flashbacks hurt</i>

00:22:30.309 --> 00:22:31.935
<i>Ever-lingering shadows</i>

00:22:31.935 --> 00:22:36.106
<i>I know I'm too bound by the past, aren't I?</i>

00:22:36.106 --> 00:22:38.525
<i>Hey, this feeling we felt</i>

00:22:38.525 --> 00:22:44.114
<i>There's no doubt about it,</i>
<i>it's got to be special</i>

00:22:44.114 --> 00:22:47.951
<i>You and me, crisscrossing emotions</i>

00:22:47.951 --> 00:22:52.164
<i>I don't want to look back with regret</i>

00:22:52.164 --> 00:22:57.002
<i>I tell myself to believe</i>

00:22:57.002 --> 00:23:00.964
<i>And I tell my heart,</i>
<i>trust me, trust me, so sparkly</i>

00:23:00.964 --> 00:23:04.760
<i>It's the rhythm of a racing pulse</i>

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:08.972
<i>As I gazed at your outstretched hand</i>

00:23:08.972 --> 00:23:15.103
<i>I decided I'd put my trust in you</i>

00:23:15.103 --> 00:23:23.529
<i>I will change myself, change myself</i>
<i>I will change myself, change myself</i>

00:23:23.529 --> 00:23:30.911
<i>I will change myself, change myself</i>
<i>I will</i>

00:23:33.789 --> 00:23:35.165
This is getting exciting!

00:23:35.165 --> 00:23:36.583
No turning back now!

00:23:36.583 --> 00:23:39.545
If we make it back alive, I'm gonna...

